  "notes": "German-produced Eurodance with a soul-inflected male lead. The one parameter the entry calls \"unusual for the lane\" is the vocal configuration — \"a single male soul-leaning lead across both verse and chorus rather than a rap/sung split, delivered forcefully and high in the chest voice\" — so the melody register drops to 57-79, a male chest band, instead of the parent's 72-96 topline, and the contour is arch-weighted for a sung line rather than riff-weighted for a stab. The drums are the entry's own: kick on all four, clap/quiet snare on 2&4, offbeat open hats, \"plus a 16th tambourine or shaker roll\", and \"fills are short snare rolls into the chorus\", which is why the snare-roll ladder and `fillBeforeSection` are both on and the roll ramp is authored. The bass moves \"in offbeat 8ths against the kick\" with the descending-bass feel the Keys line names. ⚠ The research marks the key and drum specifics `[LOW-CONF]` — they come from the genre convention, not the act — and that mark is repeated here. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are the velocity tiers, the roll ramp range and every density; the entry gives \"quiet\", \"short\" and \"forcefully\" and no numbers. Confidence is medium because the entry rates itself medium.",
